<header><h1>Maturity Payment Check</h1><p>A browser tool that checks the payment files against the trade platform data before money moves.</p></header>
<nav><div class="tabs" role="tablist" id="tabs"></div></nav>
<main>

<section id="overview" data-t="Overview">
<p class="lead">Before payments go out, this tool compares the Excel extract from the trade platform with the payment XML files, and shows PASS or FAIL for each buyer.</p>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card"><div class="big">1 + many</div>One Excel file and any number of XML payment files in</div>
<div class="card"><div class="big">3 checks</div>Control sum, transaction count and transaction amounts for every buyer</div>
<div class="card"><div class="big">0 uploads</div>Files are read inside the browser. Nothing leaves the machine.</div></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Who uses it</h3>The operations user who checks maturity payments before they are executed.</div>
<div class="card"><h3>What they get</h3>A dashboard with overall PASS/FAIL, a card for each buyer, and a drill-down from buyer to transaction to the exact invoices and XML line that explain a difference. Results can be downloaded as CSV.</div>
</section>

<section id="problem" data-t="The problem">
<p class="lead">Today the comparison is done by hand, one buyer at a time.</p>
<div class="tog" role="group" aria-label="View"><button aria-pressed="true" data-v="b">Today</button><button aria-pressed="false" data-v="a">With the utility</button></div>
<div id="vb">
<div class="card"><h3>Manual process</h3><ul><li>Build an Excel pivot for each buyer and read the totals.</li><li>Open each XML in a text editor and find the control sum, the transaction count and each amount.</li><li>Compare numbers by eye, supplier by supplier.</li></ul></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Why it hurts</h3><ul><li>Easy to miss a small difference in a large number.</li><li>Slow, and it gets slower with 30-40 buyers.</li><li>No record of what was checked or how.</li><li>The cost of a miss is a wrong payment to a customer.</li></ul></div></div>
<div id="va" hidden>
<div class="card"><h3>With the utility</h3><ul><li>Upload the files, tick the SCF buyers, click Validate.</li><li>Every check is done the same way every time, to the penny.</li><li>Failed buyers are sorted to the top, with the difference highlighted.</li><li>Drill down to see why, instead of searching through files.</li></ul></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Benefit</h3>Faster checks, fewer human errors, consistent results across the team, and a clear view of exceptions before payment.</div></div>
</section>

<section id="how" data-t="How it works">
<div class="card step"><div class="num">1</div><div><h3>Upload</h3>Drop the Excel extract and the XML files (several at once).</div></div>
<div class="card step"><div class="num">2</div><div><h3>Pick the SCF buyers</h3>The tool lists every Buyer in the Excel. Buyers whose name matches an XML debtor are pre-ticked. Unticked buyers are ignored and counted in a note.</div></div>
<div class="card step"><div class="num">3</div><div><h3>Validate</h3>One click runs all checks for every ticked buyer.</div></div>
<div class="card step"><div class="num">4</div><div><h3>Read the dashboard</h3>Overall PASS/FAIL, counts of passed and failed buyers, search, and filters.</div></div>
<div class="card step"><div class="num">5</div><div><h3>Drill down</h3>Buyer, then transaction, then the Excel invoices side by side with the XML line. <span class="tag xl">EXCEL</span> is blue and <span class="tag xm">XML</span> is purple.</div></div>
<h2 style="margin-top:20px">The three checks</h2>
<div class="card"><h3>1. Control sum</h3>Total Certified Amount for the buyer in Excel must equal <code>CtrlSum</code> in the XML.</div>
<div class="card"><h3>2. Transaction count</h3>Each Approved supplier with a non-zero total counts as 1 transaction. All Sold invoices together count as 1. The total must equal <code>NbOfTxs</code>.</div>
<div class="card"><h3>3. Transaction amounts</h3>Each Approved supplier's total must equal its XML amount (matched by name). The combined Sold total must equal the last XML transaction, whatever name it carries.</div>
<p class="small mute">A buyer passes only when all three checks pass. A ticked buyer with no XML, or an XML with no ticked buyer, fails.</p>
</section>

<section id="try" data-t="Try it">
<p class="lead">A small example with the Affiliate Supply numbers. Change the XML values and watch the checks.</p>
<div class="card"><h3><span class="tag xl">EXCEL</span> Trade platform data</h3>
<div class="wrap"><table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Supplier</th><th style="text-align:right">Certified Amount</th></tr>
<tr><td>Approved</td><td>Test Sup 2 (many invoices)</td><td style="text-align:right">5,512,000.00</td></tr>
<tr><td>Sold</td><td>Supplier One</td><td style="text-align:right">2,000,000.00</td></tr>
<tr><td>Sold</td><td>Test Sup 2</td><td style="text-align:right">1,000,000.00</td></tr></table></div>
<p class="small mute" style="margin:6px 0 0">Total 8,512,000.00. Expected transactions: 1 approved supplier + 1 combined Sold = 2.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3><span class="tag xm">XML</span> Payment file (edit these)</h3>
<label class="f">Control sum (CtrlSum)<input type="number" step="0.01" id="d0" value="8512000"></label>
<label class="f">Number of transactions (NbOfTxs)<input type="number" step="1" id="d1" value="2"></label>
<label class="f">Line 1: Test Sup 2<input type="number" step="0.01" id="d2" value="5512000"></label>
<label class="f">Last line: Lloyds Demo Funder<input type="number" step="0.01" id="d3" value="3000000"></label></div>
<button class="btn" id="r1">Reset</button><button class="btn" id="r2">Break the Sold amount by 1p</button><button class="btn" id="r3">Add a stray extra payment</button>
<div class="banner" id="db"></div><div class="card" id="dr"></div>
</section>

<section id="tech" data-t="Tech stack">
<p class="lead">A single HTML file. No server, no install, no database.</p>
<div class="card wrap"><table><tr><th>Part</th><th>Choice</th><th>Why</th></tr>
<tr><td>App</td><td>HTML, CSS and plain JavaScript</td><td>Opens in any browser; easy to share and review</td></tr>
<tr><td>Excel reading</td><td>SheetJS 0.18.5 (loaded from cdnjs)</td><td>Reads .xlsx in the browser</td></tr>
<tr><td>XML reading</td><td>Browser DOMParser</td><td>Built in; pain.001.001.03 fields read directly</td></tr>
<tr><td>Money</td><td>Whole pence as integers</td><td>No floating-point rounding errors</td></tr>
<tr><td>Export</td><td>CSV generated in the browser</td><td>No server needed</td></tr>
<tr><td>Privacy</td><td>All processing local</td><td>Bank data never uploaded</td></tr></table></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Quality so far</h3>The matching logic is a separate function, tested with scripts on sample data shaped like the ASDA, Affiliate Supply and Travis Perkins cases. It needs testing on a full real data set before reliance.</div>
<div class="card"><h3>Production options</h3><ul><li>Keep it as a single file and embed the Excel library so it works offline.</li><li>Or package it as a desktop or internal web app (for example Python with FastAPI, or a React front end) if shared storage, login and approvals are needed.</li></ul></div>
</section>

<section id="assume" data-t="Assumptions">
<p class="lead">Tap each group. These are the rules the tool follows today.</p>
<details open><summary>Excel input</summary><div><ul><li>Data is on a sheet named <code>Export</code>, or the first sheet.</li><li>Columns: Buyer, Supplier, Certified Amount, Approval Status (Invoice # and Payable # are optional).</li><li>Buyer is the program. The user ticks SCF buyers; there is no automatic SCF/RP rule yet.</li><li>All rows are read, including rows hidden by an Excel filter.</li><li>Fee, Advanced Amount, currency and dates are ignored. Everything is assumed to be GBP.</li></ul></div></details>
<details><summary>XML input</summary><div><ul><li>Files follow pain.001.001.03.</li><li>One XML covers one buyer, linked by the debtor name (<code>Dbtr/Nm</code>).</li><li>Names match after ignoring case, punctuation, "&" versus "and", and Ltd versus Limited. There is no fuzzy matching.</li></ul></div></details>
<details><summary>Validation rules</summary><div><ul><li>Amounts must match exactly, with no tolerance.</li><li>Any status containing "Sold" is Sold. All other statuses are treated as Approved.</li><li>An Approved supplier whose total is zero is not in the XML and is not counted.</li><li>All Sold invoices combine into one XML transaction, and it is the last one in the file. The name on that line is ignored.</li></ul></div></details>
<details><summary>Not covered yet</summary><div><ul><li>Duplicate records, payment date, currency and account number checks.</li><li>Fee handling (for example a small extra funder line).</li><li>Excel or PDF export, and a saved audit trail.</li></ul></div></details>
</section>

<section id="next" data-t="Next steps">
<p class="lead">Ideas in a sensible order. Each one fits in the same single file.</p>
<div class="card"><h3>Next</h3><ul><li>Embed the Excel library so it works fully offline.</li><li>Excel and PDF report with run ID, timestamp and file hashes (SHA-256).</li><li>Checker and approver name fields in the report.</li><li>One page listing all exceptions across buyers.</li></ul></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Then</h3><ul><li>Duplicate, date and currency checks.</li><li>Suggested name matches for the user to confirm.</li><li>Saved SCF/RP choices and editable rules (tolerance, statuses).</li><li>Fee handling once the rule is confirmed.</li></ul></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Later, if it becomes a shared control</h3><ul><li>Real login, maker-checker approval and a central audit log (needs a backend).</li><li>Automatic file pick-up and alerts when a check fails.</li><li>Support for other payment file formats.</li></ul></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Limits of the single file</h3>No real user login, no central tamper-proof log, no automatic pick-up from systems. Anything saved in the browser can be cleared by the user.</div>
</section>

<section id="ask" data-t="To confirm">
<p class="lead">Questions to settle with the team. Tick them off as you go.</p>
<div class="card chk">
<label><input type="checkbox"><span>How do we recognise an SCF buyer versus an RP buyer in the Excel?</span></label>
<label><input type="checkbox"><span>Is the Sold payment always the last transaction in the XML?</span></label>
<label><input type="checkbox"><span>Is the small extra funder line (for example 57.91 on Travis Perkins) a fee, and how should it be checked?</span></label>
<label><input type="checkbox"><span>Is an exact match with zero tolerance acceptable?</span></label>
<label><input type="checkbox"><span>Is one XML file always one buyer?</span></label>
<label><input type="checkbox"><span>Should payment date and currency be checked?</span></label>
<label><input type="checkbox"><span>What evidence is needed after each run (report, hashes, sign-off)?</span></label>
<label><input type="checkbox"><span>Can the tool run from a local file on work laptops, or must it be hosted internally?</span></label></div>
</section>
</main>
<script>
const $=id=>document.getElementById(id),S=[...document.querySelectorAll("section")],tb=$("tabs");
S.forEach((s,i)=>{const b=document.createElement("button");b.textContent=s.dataset.t;b.setAttribute("role","tab");b.onclick=()=>show(i);tb.appendChild(b)});
function show(i){S.forEach((s,k)=>s.classList.toggle("on",k===i));[...tb.children].forEach((b,k)=>b.setAttribute("aria-selected",k===i));tb.children[i].scrollIntoView({inline:"center",block:"nearest"});window.scrollTo({top:0})}
show(0);
document.querySelectorAll(".tog button").forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{document.querySelectorAll(".tog button").forEach(x=>x.setAttribute("aria-pressed",x===b));$("vb").hidden=b.dataset.v!=="b";$("va").hidden=b.dataset.v!=="a"});
const P=v=>Math.round((parseFloat(v)||0)*100),F=p=>(p/100).toLocaleString("en-GB",{minimumFractionDigits:2,maximumFractionDigits:2});
const T=(ok)=>`<span class="tag ${ok?"pass":"fail"}">${ok?"PASS":"FAIL"}</span>`;
function calc(){
const x=[0,1,2,3].map(i=>$("d"+i).value),ctrl=P(x[0]),nb=parseInt(x[1])||0,l1=P(x[2]),l2=P(x[3]);
const rows=[["Control sum",F(851200000),F(ctrl),ctrl===851200000],["Transaction count (1 approved + 1 sold)","2",String(nb),nb===2],["Approved: Test Sup 2",F(551200000),F(l1),l1===551200000],["Sold (combined) vs last XML line",F(300000000),F(l2),l2===300000000]];
const all=rows.every(r=>r[3]);
$("db").className="banner "+(all?"pass":"fail");$("db").textContent=all?"PASS: all checks agree":"FAIL: "+rows.filter(r=>!r[3]).length+" check(s) differ";
$("dr").innerHTML='<div class="wrap"><table><tr><th>Check</th><th style="text-align:right"><span class="tag xl">EXCEL</span></th><th style="text-align:right"><span class="tag xm">XML</span></th><th>Result</th></tr>'+rows.map(r=>`<tr><td>${r[0]}</td><td style="text-align:right">${r[1]}</td><td style="text-align:right">${r[2]}</td><td>${T(r[3])}</td></tr>`).join("")+"</table></div>";}
const set=a=>{a.forEach((v,i)=>$("d"+i).value=v);calc()};
$("r1").onclick=()=>set([8512000,2,5512000,3000000]);
$("r2").onclick=()=>set([8511999.99,2,5512000,2999999.99]);
$("r3").onclick=()=>set([8512057.91,3,5512000,3000000]);
[0,1,2,3].forEach(i=>$("d"+i).oninput=calc);calc();
</script></body></html>
